[Music]  hello everyone my name is Laura bandura  and I'm a research geophysicist at  Chevron some of you may remember that I  was on stage at Google next last July  back then I talked about how to make  sense out of way too much data we were  using Google clouds Auto ml vision API  to analyze the content of thousands of  Geoscience documents and to make them  searchable my goal then was to describe  how we could quickly access and utilize  the work documented by thousands of  Chevron employees in the form of field  reports seismic recordings core samples  lab analyses environmental studies and  much more with Google Cloud we got it in  one place digitized it and through the  power of machine learning gave this data  a new life today I want to tell you how  far we've come with that project and how  we've added tools to do something far  more valuable creating a new way of  consuming information by a diet by a  rich and diverse team of people and  acting faster to achieve our business  goals the energy business literally  powers the modern world for someone like  me part of the excitement is  understanding how we use geology and  geophysics to understand the subsurface  of the earth in my work we use seismic  waves to probe the subsurface geology  those measurements are then used to  create detailed pictures of what the  earth looks like deep into the past and  also to help us determine where oil and  gas are located here we shown an example  of a modern river system containing  channel features that have similar  dimensions and patterns to features that  we tried to find in the subsurface for  exploration and in one of these examples  is this image of a submarine canyon  system that we've found within seismic  data but the excitement doesn't stop  there the next step is to connect our  interpretations of these images to the  value chain and to ultimately impact how  we produce oil and gas  for an integrated energy company like  Chevron that mean that means working  